Related: #158318. This addresses the explicit wait/cancellation path; it does not close the broader ingress and blocker-diagnostics request.

## What Problem This Solves

Targeted plugin reload gives up after 60 seconds even when healthy admitted work will finish shortly afterward, leaving operators to retry manually.

## User Impact

Operators can run `openclaw plugins reload <ids...> --wait` to wait for admitted work without restarting the Gateway. The default remains 60 seconds. Ctrl+C or requester disconnect cancels the pre-publication wait; admitted runs continue, and rollback restores dispatch when recovery succeeds. Cancellation after publication does not undo the new generation. Cleanup and recovery retain their existing deadlines.

Existing channel queue/replay guarantees remain unchanged. This does not add crash-durable ingress, identify leaked retention tokens, or make a reload invoked from a turn holding the same plugin able to finish itself. Run maintenance outside that turn.

## Why This Change Was Made

The reload owner now controls one abortable settlement observation instead of repeatedly applying five-second observers inside a sixty-second retry loop. Its signal reaches retained work, active calls, and finite consumers. Request cancellation is separate from Gateway-owned recovery and physical lease release. CLI and RPC use the same lifecycle transaction; the optional wire field also updates generated Swift models.

Production delta: +40 lines (190 added  / 150 removed), excluding generated output. The added capability is requester-owned cancellable waiting across CLI/RPC/lifecycle boundaries; the cleanup owner itself shrinks by 14 lines. Tests: +354 net; docs: +14; generated Swift: +4. Existing lifecycle plan construction moves to its plan owner, and its propagation regression moves out of the oversized main config suite.

## Evidence

Real packaged Gateway on Node 24.19.0; actual Anthropic plugin/CLI lifecycle and QA channel admission, with a deterministic fake Claude stdio executable and QA message bus. This is not an authenticated external-channel/model test. Same frozen harness on base `9bb0e452d9bb6f55947bb984fa1125af6a04b785` and candidate: one 85-second admitted turn; three independent account/session arrivals injected only after the reload owner reports its gate. Both use a canonical physical temporary state path.

| Observation | Base/default | Candidate/explicit wait |
|---|---:|---:|
| First reload | Failed after 60,463 ms | Applied after 87,624 ms |
| First generation transition | 2→2 | 2→3 |
| Identified replies | 4/4, each exactly once | 4/4, each exactly once |
| New arrivals | Held about 60s, resumed on rollback | Started after initial work finished and replacement published |
| Gateway PID | Unchanged | Unchanged |
| HTTP health | 89/89 returned 200 | 96/96 returned 200 |
| Final owned-process cleanup | Confirmed stopped; no errors | Confirmed stopped; no errors |

Separate candidate cancellation run: disconnect the reload request at 70,003 ms while the original 85-second turn is still running. The three queued replies resume within 1,842 ms, generation stays 2, original work finishes normally, all 4 replies arrive exactly once, all 88 health checks return 200, and retry publishes generation 3 without changing PID. This exercises a real RPC disconnect; CLI signal/exit behavior is covered separately by regression tests, not claimed as an empirical SIGINT run.

Validation:
- New pre-fix owner cases failed at 70s; repaired retained-token, retained-consumer, and active-call cases cover completion and cancellation beyond 60s.
- Recovery + installed-package suites: 113 passed; instance/consumer and prepared-runtime resource suites: 83 passed.
- Full CLI/management/config/WebSocket selection: 596 passed; after moving lifecycle plan construction, both config suites: 493 passed. After final test lint corrections, affected recovery/observation/CLI suites: 133 passed. Counts overlap; they are not a unique-test total.
- Cancellation regressions cover before/after publication and a real SQLite lifecycle lease remaining held until physical rollback settles.
- Core and 25 core-test typecheck groups, scoped lint, selected repository boundary/dead-export/architecture guards, protocol generation/check, and full private-QA build completed. The strict UI startup budget fails on both revisions using the same toolchain and build identity: baseline 371,513 B; candidate 371,561 B (+48 B); limit 371,332 B. The general build reports this budget without failing. This pre-existing budget overage remains a named follow-up; no budget threshold was raised.
- Independent Codex autoreview: scoped-clean through P2. It reviewed the frozen code; real Gateway observations above were collected afterward.

### Connection to earlier reload changes

Our [#149675](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/149675) introduced this shared resource-handoff/cleanup owner. Later [#151273](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/151273) introduced the sixty-second pre-stop admitted-work policy, and [#157796](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/157796) enabled waiting behind retained work and supplied the queued-work message. The exact timeout policy is therefore later than our original reload stack, while the code shares that earlier architecture. The reproduction demonstrates a legitimate long turn timing out, not a proven retention leak. Hannes's exact commit and original eight holders remain unknown; a package version string alone does not establish that attribution.

### Named follow-up: macOS aliased state-directory ownership during concurrent session writes

An initial /tmp-based run hit SQLite backend-ownership conflicts and two missing replies after reload rollback. A no-reload control reproduced the ownership conflict but delivered all four replies. Using a canonical physical temporary root removed those conflicts in the paired runs while preserving the baseline 60-second reload failure. Source suggests lexical path aliases select competing execution owners for one physical database; the cause of the two missing replies remains unproven. These failures are retained as a separate investigation, not claimed fixed by this patch.

<details><summary>Reproduce the paired real-Gateway scenario</summary>

Save the following as `test/e2e/qa-lab/runtime/reload-158318-retained-work.proof.mts` before building. Use the same installed dependencies and Node24 toolchain on each revision. Build with `OPENCLAW_BUILD_PRIVATE_QA=1 pnpm build`. From the repository root run:

```sh
env -u OPENCLAW_DEV_SOURCE_ROOT node --import ./scripts/tsx.mjs test/e2e/qa-lab/runtime/reload-158318-retained-work.proof.mts
# On the candidate, select the explicit wait:
env -u OPENCLAW_DEV_SOURCE_ROOT OPENCLAW_RELOAD_PROOF_PARAMS='{"plugins":[{"pluginId":"anthropic"}],"waitForDrain":true}' node --import ./scripts/tsx.mjs test/e2e/qa-lab/runtime/reload-158318-retained-work.proof.mts
```

The harness records observations and cleanup in its temporary evidence directory. Inspect the verdict's reload result, generation, deliveryCounts, turn timestamps, health samples, and cleanup; process exit alone is not the delivery assertion.

```typescript
import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
import fs from 'node:fs';
import os from 'node:os';
import path from 'node:path';
import { setTimeout as delay } from 'node:timers/promises';
import { execFileSync } from 'node:child_process';
import { createQaBusState, createQaChannelTransport, startQaBusServer } from '../../../../extensions/qa-lab/api.js';
import { createQaLiveLaneGateway } from '../../../../extensions/qa-lab/runtime-api.js';

const FAKE_CLAUDE = "#!/usr/bin/env node\n// Minimal claude-stdio protocol: initialize handshake, one user turn, delayed result.\nconst fs = require(\"node:fs\");\nconst path = require(\"node:path\");\nconst { createInterface } = require(\"node:readline\");\nconst dir = process.env.FAKE_CLAUDE_DIR;\nconst log = (line) => fs.appendFileSync(path.join(dir, \"fake-claude.log\"), new Date().toISOString() + \" pid=\" + process.pid + \" \" + line + \"\\n\");\nconst argv = process.argv.slice(2);\nif (argv.includes(\"--version\")) { process.stdout.write(\"2.1.300 (Claude Code)\\n\"); process.exit(0); }\nif (argv[0] === \"auth\" && argv[1] === \"status\") {\n  process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify({ loggedIn: true, authMethod: \"claude.ai\", email: \"qa@example.com\" }) + \"\\n\");\n  process.exit(0);\n}\nlog(\"spawn argv=\" + JSON.stringify(argv));\nconst send = (value) => process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify(value) + \"\\n\");\nconst sessionIdx = argv.indexOf(\"--session-id\");\nconst sessionId = sessionIdx >= 0 ? argv[sessionIdx + 1] : require(\"node:crypto\").randomUUID();\nconst turnMs = Number(process.env.FAKE_CLAUDE_TURN_MS || \"85000\");\nlet resultEmitted = false;\nfor (const sig of [\"SIGTERM\", \"SIGINT\", \"SIGHUP\"]) {\n  process.on(sig, () => { log(\"signal \" + sig + (resultEmitted ? \" (exit)\" : \" (ignored, turn in flight)\")); if (resultEmitted) process.exit(0); });\n}\nprocess.stdin.on(\"end\", () => { log(\"stdin end\"); if (resultEmitted) process.exit(0); });\nsetInterval(() => {}, 60_000);\nconst rl = createInterface({ input: process.stdin });\nrl.on(\"line\", (line) => {\n  let message;\n  try { message = JSON.parse(line); } catch { log(\"non-json line bytes=\" + line.length); return; }\n  if (message.type === \"control_request\" && message.request && message.request.subtype === \"initialize\") {\n    log(\"initialize received\");\n    send({ type: \"control_response\", response: { subtype: \"success\", request_id: message.request_id, response: { commands: [], models: [] } } });\n    return;\n  }\n  if (message.type === \"control_request\") {\n    log(\"control_request subtype=\" + (message.request && message.request.subtype) + \" request_id=\" + message.request_id);\n    send({ type: \"control_response\", response: { subtype: \"success\", request_id: message.request_id, response: {} } });\n    return;\n  }\n  if (message.type === \"control_cancel_request\") { log(\"control_cancel_request \" + message.request_id); return; }\n  if (message.type === \"user\") {\n    const content = message.message && message.message.content;\n    log(\"user turn received uuid=\" + message.uuid + \" contentHead=\" + JSON.stringify(String(typeof content === \"string\" ? content : JSON.stringify(content)).slice(0, 120)));\n    const proofId = JSON.stringify(content).match(/RELOADPROOF_[A-Z0-9_]+/)?.[0] || \"unidentified\";\n    fs.appendFileSync(path.join(dir, \"turns.jsonl\"), JSON.stringify({ event: \"start\", proofId, pid: process.pid, at: Date.now() }) + \"\\n\");\n    send({ type: \"system\", subtype: \"init\", session_id: sessionId, model: \"claude-opus-5\", tools: [], cwd: process.cwd() });\n    setTimeout(() => {\n      const text = \"reply \" + proofId;\n      send({ type: \"assistant\", message: { id: \"msg_1\", role: \"assistant\", model: \"claude-opus-5\", content: [{ type: \"text\", text }] }, session_id: sessionId });\n      send({ type: \"result\", subtype: \"success\", is_error: false, result: text, session_id: sessionId, duration_ms: turnMs, num_turns: 1, usage: { input_tokens: 10, output_tokens: 5 } });\n      resultEmitted = true;\n      log(\"turn finished (result emitted)\");\n      fs.appendFileSync(path.join(dir, \"turns.jsonl\"), JSON.stringify({ event: \"finish\", proofId, pid: process.pid, at: Date.now() }) + \"\\n\");\n    }, proofId === \"RELOADPROOF_INITIAL\" ? turnMs : 100);\n    return;\n  }\n  log(\"other message type=\" + message.type);\n});\n";
const evidenceRoot = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), 'openclaw-158318-gateway-'));
const fakeDir = path.join(evidenceRoot, 'fake-cli');
fs.mkdirSync(fakeDir);
fs.writeFileSync(path.join(fakeDir, 'claude'), FAKE_CLAUDE, { mode: 0o755 });
const record: Record<string, unknown> = {
  evidenceRoot,
  source: execFileSync('git', ['rev-parse', 'HEAD'], { encoding: 'utf8' }).trim(),
  node: process.version,
  canonicalTempParent: fs.realpathSync(os.tmpdir()),
  fixture: 'Real Gateway and channel admission; QA bus and fake claude stdio model; 85 second admitted initial turn',
};
function emit(event: string, value: unknown) {
  const observation = { event, at: new Date().toISOString(), value };
  fs.appendFileSync(path.join(evidenceRoot, 'observations.jsonl'), JSON.stringify(observation) + '\n');
  console.log('RELOAD_158318_PROOF ' + JSON.stringify(observation));
}
function turns(): Array<{event: string; proofId: string; pid: number; at: number}> {
  const file = path.join(fakeDir, 'turns.jsonl');
  return fs.existsSync(file) ? fs.readFileSync(file, 'utf8').trim().split('\n').filter(Boolean).map(line => JSON.parse(line)) : [];
}
async function waitFor<T>(name: string, probe: () => T | undefined | Promise<T | undefined>, budget = 120_000): Promise<T> {
  const deadline = Date.now() + budget;
  while (Date.now() < deadline) {
    const result = await probe();
    if (result !== undefined) return result;
    await delay(100);
  }
  throw new Error('Timed out: ' + name);
}
const state = createQaBusState();
const bus = await startQaBusServer({ state });
const owner = createQaLiveLaneGateway();
let gateway: Awaited<ReturnType<typeof owner.start>>['gateway'] | undefined;
let healthTimer: ReturnType<typeof setInterval> | undefined;
const health: unknown[] = [];
const expected = ['RELOADPROOF_INITIAL', 'RELOADPROOF_DURING_1', 'RELOADPROOF_DURING_2', 'RELOADPROOF_DURING_3'];
function send(proofId: string) {
  state.addInboundMessage({ accountId: proofId === 'RELOADPROOF_INITIAL' ? 'default' : proofId.toLowerCase(), conversation: { kind: 'direct', id: proofId }, senderId: proofId, text: proofId });
  emit('ingress', { proofId });
}
try {
  const harness = await owner.start({
    repoRoot: process.cwd(), command: { executablePath: process.execPath, argsPrefix: [path.join(process.cwd(), 'dist/index.js')], cwd: process.cwd(), usePackagedPlugins: true, tempParentDir: fs.realpathSync(os.tmpdir()) }, providerMode: 'mock-openai', primaryModel: 'mock-openai/gpt-5.6-luna', alternateModel: 'mock-openai/gpt-5.6-luna-alt',
    transport: createQaChannelTransport(state), transportBaseUrl: bus.baseUrl, controlUiEnabled: false,
    runtimeEnvPatch: { PATH: `${fakeDir}${path.delimiter}${process.env.PATH ?? ''}`, FAKE_CLAUDE_DIR: fakeDir, FAKE_CLAUDE_TURN_MS: '85000' },
    mutateConfig: cfg => ({ ...cfg,
      session: { ...cfg.session, dmScope: 'per-channel-peer' },
      channels: { ...cfg.channels, 'qa-channel': { ...cfg.channels?.['qa-channel'], accounts: { default: {}, reloadproof_during_1: {}, reloadproof_during_2: {}, reloadproof_during_3: {} } } },
      plugins: { ...cfg.plugins, allow: [...new Set([...(cfg.plugins?.allow ?? []), 'anthropic'])], entries: { ...cfg.plugins?.entries, anthropic: { enabled: true } } },
      agents: { ...cfg.agents, defaults: { ...cfg.agents?.defaults, maxConcurrent: 8, model: 'claude-cli/claude-opus-5', models: { ...cfg.agents?.defaults?.models, 'claude-cli/claude-opus-5': {} }, modelPolicy: { allow: [...(cfg.agents?.defaults?.modelPolicy?.allow ?? []), 'claude-cli/claude-opus-5'] } }, entries: { ...cfg.agents?.entries, qa: { ...cfg.agents?.entries?.qa, model: 'claude-cli/claude-opus-5' } } }
    })
  });
  gateway = harness.gateway;
  async function snapshot() {
    const result = await gateway!.call('plugins.list', {}) as { generation: number; plugins: Array<{ id: string; runtime: unknown }> };
    return { generation: result.generation, plugins: result.plugins.filter(p => ['anthropic', 'qa-channel', 'qa-lab'].includes(p.id)).map(p => ({ id: p.id, runtime: p.runtime })) };
  }
  const pid = gateway.pid;
  record.pidBefore = pid;
  record.gatewayTempRoot = gateway.tempRoot;
  emit('ready', { pid, tempRoot: gateway.tempRoot });
  healthTimer = setInterval(() => {
    void fetch(`${gateway!.baseUrl}/health`).then(res => { health.push({ at: Date.now(), status: res.status }); }, err => { health.push({ at: Date.now(), error: String(err) }); });
  }, 1000);
  record.pluginsBefore = await snapshot();
  send(expected[0]);
  await waitFor('initial CLI turn admitted', () => turns().find(t => t.event === 'start' && t.proofId === expected[0]));
  emit('initial-admitted', turns());
  const startedAt = Date.now();
  const request = JSON.parse(process.env.OPENCLAW_RELOAD_PROOF_PARAMS ?? '{"plugins":[{"pluginId":"anthropic"}]}');
  const reload = gateway.call('plugins.reload', request, { timeoutMs: 180_000 }).then(
    result => ({ ok: true, elapsedMs: Date.now() - startedAt, result }),
    error => ({ ok: false, elapsedMs: Date.now() - startedAt, error: String(error) }),
  );
  emit('reload-request', request);
  // Observe the owner log before injecting concurrent ingress, rather than a scheduling sleep.
  await waitFor('reload reached owner or completed', async () => {
    const logs = gateway!.logs();
    if (logs.includes('Plugin replacement queued behind')) return true;
    return undefined;
  }, 20_000);
  for (const id of expected.slice(1)) send(id);
  record.reload = await reload;
  emit('reload-result', record.reload);
  record.turnsAtReloadResult = turns();
  record.pluginsAfterFirstReload = await snapshot();
  await waitFor('initial CLI completed', () => turns().find(t => t.event === 'finish' && t.proofId === expected[0]), 120_000);
  await waitFor('all identified replies', () => expected.every(id => state.getSnapshot().messages.some(m => m.direction === 'outbound' && m.text === 'reply ' + id)) ? true : undefined, 120_000).catch(error => { record.deliveryWaitError = String(error); });
  record.turns = turns();
  record.messages = state.getSnapshot().messages.map(m => ({ direction: m.direction, text: m.text }));
  record.deliveryCounts = Object.fromEntries(expected.map(id => [id, state.getSnapshot().messages.filter(m => m.direction === 'outbound' && m.text === 'reply ' + id).length]));
  record.retryAfterCompletion = await gateway.call('plugins.reload', { plugins: [{ pluginId: 'anthropic' }] }, { timeoutMs: 180_000 }).then(result => ({ ok: true, result }), error => ({ ok: false, error: String(error) }));
  record.pluginsAfterRetry = await snapshot();
  record.pidAfter = gateway.pid;
  record.health = health;
  assert.equal(gateway.pid, pid, 'Gateway process did not restart');
  emit('observed', record);
} catch (error) {
  record.failure = String(error);
  emit('failure', { error: String(error), logs: gateway?.logs() });
  process.exitCode = 1;
} finally {
  if (healthTimer) clearInterval(healthTimer);
  if (gateway) fs.writeFileSync(path.join(evidenceRoot, 'gateway.log'), gateway.logs());
  const preserved = path.join(process.cwd(), '.artifacts', 'qa-e2e', path.basename(evidenceRoot));
  const stopped = await owner.stop({ preserveToDir: preserved });
  if (fs.existsSync(preserved)) {
    fs.cpSync(preserved, path.join(evidenceRoot, 'gateway-artifacts'), { recursive: true });
    fs.rmSync(preserved, { recursive: true });
  }
  record.cleanup = { process: stopped.process, errors: stopped.errors.map(String) };
  await bus.stop();
  fs.writeFileSync(path.join(evidenceRoot, 'verdict.json'), JSON.stringify(record, null, 2));
  emit('cleanup', record.cleanup);
  console.log('RELOAD_158318_VERDICT ' + JSON.stringify(record));
  if (stopped.errors.length) process.exitCode = 1;
}

